course: dictionary
lesson: 12955
title: Excitable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Excitable describes someone or something that gets excited very easily. A person or animal who is excitable gets wound up quickly and finds it hard to calm down.
explain: Read the words around it for clues. «The excitable puppy jumped at every visitor and barked.» Jumping and barking show that the puppy gets excited fast. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The easily excited puppy jumped at every visitor» still makes sense.
explain: Excitable can also mean nervous or upset very easily. «Ella is excitable before a test, and she keeps checking her bag.» Here Ella gets nervous quickly, so excitable means more than just happy.
fact: Excitable means getting excited, nervous or upset very easily.
fact: «An excitable puppy» is a puppy that gets wound up quickly.
fact: Excitable is an adjective. Its comparative form is more excitable.
fact: Easily excitable means the same as excitable, as in «Max is easily excitable».
fact: Excited is a feeling you have right now. Excitable describes a person or animal who is likely to get that way.
exercise: «The excitable puppy wagged its tail and yapped at everyone.» What does excitable describe? | A puppy that cannot see | *A puppy that gets wound up quickly | A puppy that is fast asleep | A puppy that is very old
exercise: Mia says excitable means calm. Which is correct? | It means very tall | It means sleepy | *It means getting excited, nervous or upset very easily | It means calm and quiet
exercise: «Ben gets excitable before a football match.» What does this sentence tell you about Ben? | He is very tall for his age | *He gets excited or nervous quickly | He always falls asleep before games | He never plays football
test: «On his birthday, the excitable dog ran around the garden three times.» What does excitable mean here? | Very slow and sleepy | Very clean | Lost and frightened of the dark | *Gets wound up and excited quickly
test: Which use shows someone getting upset easily? | «The excitable cat slept in the sun.» | *«The excitable boy shook and cried when the thunder started.» | «She reads a book quietly every night.» | «He ate his lunch under the tree.»
exam: What is the best meaning of excitable? | *Easily excited, nervous or upset | Quiet and calm all the time | Very old and slow | Lost and far from home
</br>
